                "new_text": "# Reconciling `origin/main` into `downstream/sf_triggers`\n\n## Context\n\n`downstream/sf_triggers` branched off `main` at `d07c10a`. Since then `main`\nhas picked up 14 commits (through `204958f`) that fix a real bug in the LoRA\nfine-tuning path shared by every downstream app, add config-load-time\nvalidation, and add a test suite \u2014 while `sf_triggers` has 6 commits of its\nown building out the sf_triggers app itself, plus a pile of **uncommitted**\nlocal edits to the two shared infra files main also touched. Those local\nedits turn out to be an independent, partial fix for the *same* bug main\nfixed, using a different mechanism. The goal is to pull main's fixes in\nwithout losing the sf_triggers-specific work, and to resolve the one real\noverlap deliberately rather than by whichever way `git merge` happens to\nfall.\n\n`git merge-tree d07c10a HEAD origin/main` shows **no conflicts at the commit\nlevel** \u2014 sf_triggers's committed history only touches files under\n`downstream_apps/sf_triggers/`, which main never touches. The only frictions\ncome from the *uncommitted* working-tree changes (see below).\n\n## What changed on `main` (d07c10a..origin/main, 14 commits)\n\n**1. LoRA bug fix (the important one) \u2014 `workshop_infrastructure/utils.py`, `workshop_infrastructure/models/finetune_models.py`, `workshop_infrastructure/configs.py`, `downstream_apps/template/*`**\n\nTwo independent bugs in the shared LoRA path, both silent (loss still went\ndown):\n- `LoraAdapterConfig.target_modules` listed `q_proj/v_proj/k_proj/out_proj`,\n  which don't exist on the vendored backbone (it fuses q/k/v into\n  `attn.qkv`, and the output projection is `attn.proj`). Only `fc1`/`fc2`\n  were ever actually adapted. Fixed default: `[fc1, fc2, attn.qkv, attn.proj]`.\n- `apply_peft_lora()` passed no `modules_to_save` to PEFT, so the entire\n  fine-tuning head (pooling layer, cls token, unembed/decoder) was frozen at\n  its random initialization the whole time. Fixed by a new **`head_` naming\n  convention**: every trainable head component must be a direct child\n  attribute named `head_*` (`head_linear`, `head_unembed`, `head_cls_token`,\n  \u2026); a new `discover_head_modules()` in `utils.py` finds them and passes\n  them to PEFT as `modules_to_save`, and raises an actionable error if the\n  convention is violated. `finetune_models.py` was renamed throughout\n  (`unembed`\u2192`head_unembed`, `cls_token`\u2192`head_cls_token`, etc.), and a new\n  `ClassToken` wrapper module was added so a bare token `nn.Parameter` can be\n  covered too.\n- README.md/CLAUDE.md/ADAPTING.md carry an explicit **\"results from before\n  this fix are invalid, re-run any LoRA experiment\"** warning, and note that\n  old checkpoints saved under the old attribute names can no longer be\n  loaded.\n- Side effect: `ModelConfig.nglo` field removed \u2014 `HelioSpectformer1D` now\n  derives `nglo` internally from `pooling` (1 for `class_token`, else 0)\n  instead of taking it from config.\n\n**2. Config validation \u2014 `workshop_infrastructure/configs.py`**\nNew `ModelConfig.__post_init__` checks (`img_size` % `patch_size`,\n`spectral_blocks` range, `checkpoint_layers` range, `learned_flow` vs\n`time_embedding.type`) and new `TrainingConfig.__post_init__` checks\n(`deterministic: true` + `learned_flow: true` incompatibility,\n`time_embedding.time_dim` vs `len(data.time_delta_input_minutes)`). These\nare \"unknown keys raise\"-style hard failures at load time, not warnings.\n\n**3. New test suite \u2014 `tests/` (new directory)**\n`conftest.py`, `test_lora_setup.py`, `test_model_config.py` \u2014 pins the\ntrainable-parameter counts for all three fine-tuning regimes and the\nconfig validations above. Repo-root level, not per-app.\n\n**4. Misc**\n- `requirements.txt` (new, root-level pip freeze of runtime deps).\n- `.gitignore`: adds `*.json`, `unified_report.md`, `variance_accounting.txt`.\n- `downstream_apps/template/{2_finetune_template_1D.ipynb,3_finetune_template_1D.py,ADAPTING.md,configs/config_script.yaml}`\n  \u2014 the template's own copies updated to match the LoRA fix (comments,\n  `target_modules`, dropped `nglo: 1`).\n- `CLAUDE.md`, `README.md` \u2014 documentation updated to describe all of the above.\n\n## What's already true on `downstream/sf_triggers`\n\n- `workshop_infrastructure/models/finetune_models.py` \u2014 **uncommitted local\n  edit is byte-for-byte identical to main's version.** No work needed here\n  beyond taking main's version (or keeping the local one \u2014 they match).\n- `workshop_infrastructure/utils.py` \u2014 **uncommitted local edit fixes the\n  same head-frozen bug, differently.** Instead of `discover_head_modules()` +\n  PEFT `modules_to_save`, it adds a manual loop after `get_peft_model()`\n  that sets `requires_grad = True` on every parameter outside `backbone.*`\n  that isn't a LoRA adapter. This works *because* `finetune_models.py` was\n  already renamed to `head_*`, but it duplicates main's mechanism with a\n  cruder one (no `discover_head_modules` validation, no `[LoRA] Adapted\n  modules` logging, no collision/bare-parameter checks). **This is the one\n  real decision point** \u2014 see questions below.\n- `workshop_infrastructure/configs.py` \u2014 **not touched locally at all**,\n  still has the stale `nglo: int = 1` field and the old broken\n  `target_modules` default, and is missing all the new `__post_init__`\n  validation. Needs main's version.\n- `downstream_apps/sf_triggers/configs/config_script.yaml` (uncommitted) \u2014\n  already manually patched to `target_modules: [fc1, fc2, attn.qkv,\n  attn.proj]` (matches main's fix) and has `# nglo: 1` commented out\n  (harmless either way once `configs.py` drops the field). Also has\n  unrelated local experiment tweaks (`r: 2`, `batch_size: 1`) \u2014 not part of\n  reconciliation, left alone.\n- `downstream_apps/sf_triggers/3_finetune_template_1D.py` (uncommitted) \u2014\n  already has the comment update, and separately mid-flight on an unrelated\n  change (swapping `HelioSpectformer1D` \u2192 `HelioSpectformer2D`, new dataset\n  kwargs `ds_val_fraction`/`ds_split_seed`/`mask_dir`/`mask_time_tolerance`).\n  That's the user's own current feature work, orthogonal to this\n  reconciliation \u2014 do not touch it beyond whatever the merge naturally does.\n- No sf_triggers-specific tests exist; the new `tests/` directory is\n  repo-generic and doesn't need an sf_triggers counterpart.\n- `downstream_apps/sf_triggers/ADAPTING.md` (371 lines, sf_triggers's own,\n  not shared) predates the LoRA fix narrative \u2014 optional follow-up to port\n  the same warnings into it, not required for correctness.\n\n## Practical implication for this branch\n\nBecause sf_triggers's LoRA runs to date used both bugs (broken\n`target_modules` *and* a frozen head, until the still-uncommitted local\nfixes), main's \"re-run any LoRA experiment done before this fix\" warning\napplies here too. Worth flagging even though it's not a code change.\n\n## Proposed reconciliation steps\n\n1. Decide the two open questions below.\n2. Commit or stash the current uncommitted changes on `downstream/sf_triggers`\n   (git merge will otherwise refuse to touch files with local modifications\n   that main also changed \u2014 `utils.py`, `finetune_models.py`,\n   `config_script.yaml`, `3_finetune_template_1D.py`, the notebook).\n3. `git merge origin/main` (confirmed conflict-free at the commit level via\n   `git merge-tree`).\n4. Reapply/reconcile the uncommitted work on top:\n   - `finetune_models.py`: no-op, already matches.\n   - `utils.py`: per the decision in Q2 below.\n   - `config_script.yaml`: keep the local `target_modules` override (now\n     redundant with the new default, harmless) and the unrelated `r`/\n     `batch_size` experiment values; drop the now-fully-dead `# nglo: 1`\n     comment line.\n   - `3_finetune_template_1D.py` / notebook: keep the sf_triggers-specific\n     `HelioSpectformer2D` work as-is.\n5. Run `pytest tests/ -v` and a capped (`max_samples`) training run to\n   confirm the merged `configs.py` validations don't reject sf_triggers's\n   config.\n\n## Open questions\n\n1. **utils.py fix**: adopt main's `discover_head_modules()` +\n   `modules_to_save` mechanism (recommended \u2014 tested, validated, logs what's\n   trainable), or keep the local manual `requires_grad` loop since it\n   already works?\n2. **Uncommitted work**: commit it as a checkpoint before merging, or stash\n   it, or something else?\n",
                "path": "/home/jovyan/.claude/plans/the-main-branch-in-expressive-babbage.md"
              }
            ],
