      "time": 1789671193.1732252,
      "type": "msg",
      "body": "I've compared `downstream/sf_triggers` against `origin/main` (14 commits ahead, `d07c10a` \u2192 `204958f`). Summary:\n\n**Main's changes, grouped:**\n1. **LoRA bug fix (the big one)** \u2014 two silent bugs in the shared fine-tuning path: `target_modules` referenced layer names (`q_proj`/`k_proj`/`v_proj`/`out_proj`) that don't exist on the vendored backbone (only `fc1`/`fc2`/`attn.qkv`/`attn.proj` do \u2014 so attention was never actually adapted), and `apply_peft_lora()` never told PEFT to keep the fine-tuning head trainable, so the head trained from its random init the whole time. Fixed via a new `head_*` naming convention + `discover_head_modules()` in `utils.py`, plus renames throughout `finetune_models.py` (`unembed`\u2192`head_unembed`, etc.) and a new `ClassToken` wrapper. Main's docs explicitly warn: **any LoRA run before this fix is invalid, re-run it.**\n2. **New config-load validation** in `workshop_infrastructure/configs.py` (`img_size`/`patch_size`, `spectral_blocks`/`depth`, `checkpoint_layers` range, `deterministic`+`learned_flow` conflict, `time_dim` vs `time_delta_input_minutes`), plus the `ModelConfig.nglo` field being removed (now derived from `pooling`).\n3. **New `tests/` suite** (repo-root, generic) pinning the trainable-param counts and validations above.\n4. Misc: new root `requirements.txt`, `.gitignore` additions, and the `downstream_apps/template/` copies + `CLAUDE.md`/`README.md` updated to match.\n\n**What's already true on this branch** (checked via diffs, not assumed):\n- Your *uncommitted* `finetune_models.py` is byte-identical to main's \u2014 already done.\n- Your *uncommitted* `utils.py` fixes the same \"head frozen under LoRA\" bug, but differently: a manual `requires_grad = True` loop over non-backbone params, instead of main's `discover_head_modules()`/`modules_to_save`. This is the one real overlap to decide on.\n- Your *uncommitted* `configs/config_script.yaml` already has the corrected `target_modules`.\n- `workshop_infrastructure/configs.py` hasn't been touched locally at all \u2014 still has the stale `nglo` field and old `target_modules` default, and is missing all the new validation.\n- No conflicts at the commit level (`git merge-tree` confirms) \u2014 only friction is that several files with the overlap above are currently dirty/uncommitted.\n\nFull detail is in the plan file. Two things I need from you before touching anything:\n\n1. For `utils.py` \u2014 adopt main's `discover_head_modules()` + PEFT `modules_to_save` approach (tested, validated, logs what's trainable), or keep your manual `requires_grad` loop since it already works?\n2. For your uncommitted work \u2014 want me to commit it as a checkpoint before merging main, or stash it, or handle it some other way?",
